                                                "sense_id": "23afe46d-dccf-3321-9308-a42caefa7bf0",
                                                "text": "Yet these increasingly hypertrophic forms of masculinity existed in tension with ideals of obedience, courtesy, cultural refinement and charity that were still viewed as markers of the ‘gentleman’."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7fd2b24a-baad-3f3f-92b4-b64796f6d2c0",
                                        "entry_id": "77acf6b2-aac4-3470-ae6d-38bae82270f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, pertaining to, or exhibiting hypertrophy.",
                                            "Raised but not to the extent of a keloid. Hypertrophic scars stay within the original area of a wound, while keloids extend beyond."
                                        ],
